This can lead to boot loops when too many cores draw current at the same time.
A USB-C splitter can be used to split the single USB-C port into separate data and power ports.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Connect to UART</title><link>https://opencca.github.io/docs/reference/rk3588/connect-to-uart/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 Aug 2025 16:04:48 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://opencca.github.io/docs/reference/rk3588/connect-to-uart/</guid><description>&lt;p>Connect to TX, RX and GND to the TTL usb adapter (we need 3.3V).&lt;/p>
